docs/nit-269-handoff.md:143:- `TAILOR_PROVIDER=mock` is the default and the only provider used by `npm test`, `npm run test:ui` and `npm run dev`. The mock (`src/clients/neatlogs/mock-provider.ts`, over the generic offline shell in `src/tailor/mock-provider.ts`) is heuristic: it recognises a bounded set of domains and failure shapes, so "unfamiliar wording" works to the extent the heuristics cover it. The UI labels this honestly ("Mock-backed" chip; "Mock-backed prototype — no live model yet"), now from the server's `GET /api/execution` on every page. A live run is the separate, approval-gated `npm run dev:live`, and never falls back to the mock.
