docs/nit-269-handoff.md:170:Per turn: one planning call (interpret, choose a supported action, propose a scenario or ask one three-choice clarification) and, after a successful save and read-back, one explanation call that receives only the read-back evidence. Knowledge retrieval, permissions, schema/timing/relationship validation, persistence, version checks and read-back stay in deterministic code; model output is validated structurally and grounded before use. Refusals (`stop_reason: refusal`), truncation (`max_tokens`), malformed output, context-window overflow, 401/403/402, 429, 529, timeouts and network errors are mapped to a `ProviderErrorKind`, recorded in telemetry (`provider_error_kind`, `retryable`, `request_id`) and surfaced to the buyer as a generic "nothing changed" reply. Refuse and unsupported prose passes the same claim filters as answers, so invented prices, plans and capabilities are dropped. Timeouts: see "Timeouts" above (60 s per call, 90 s turn deadline, no in-turn retry of timeouts).
